 "title": "Landfall",
 "dates": "Friday, October 9 – Monday, October 12, 2009",
 "logline": "Wes Arceneaux flies west to see the Pacific, Jack brings Becca to everything, and Theo and Laney host the longest weekend of the fall.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "“Do you know what you’re doing yet?” You said Becca’s nice. Sweet. She laughed. “You look relieved.” “I’m not relieved.”",
   "if": "e8_relief==\"named\""
  },
  {
   "text": "“Do you know what you’re doing yet?” You didn’t. You said Becca’s nice. Sweet. She laughed before she could stop it.",
   "if": "e8_relief!=\"named\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the Delgado elevator, four in the morning: “That was a terrible thing to be glad about.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lena mailed Wes a jar of the Pacific. “Luc says it smells like bait. Wes says it smells like me.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "You asked Becca out, and you paid: the elephant seals at Piedras Blancas at sunset. On the Portolá steps, you kissed her.",
   "if": "e8_date==\"seals\" && e8_becca_end==\"kiss\""
  },
  {
   "text": "You asked Becca out for Friday, and you paid. “Nobody’s ever planned a thing for me. I’m the one who plans the thing.”",
   "if": "e8_date!=\"seals\" || e8_becca_end!=\"kiss\""
  },
  {
   "text": "From the Dome, in capitals: “WHO DAT 4-0!!! 5 DAYS. TELL THE OHIO GUY WHO DAT.”",
   "if": "e8_sun==\"sullys\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Two floors down, Sunday night, on the phone to New Orleans: “Five days.”",
   "if": "e8_sun!=\"sullys\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Sunday, ten past six in the morning, Theo in wet jeans: “I run now. Four miles. Barefoot.”"
  }
 ],
